**Given:**

Debt (Principal) = ₹28,700

Rate of interest (r) = 5% p.a.

Time (n) = 2 years

**Formula used:**

The annual equal payment (A) for discharging a loan is calculated using the formula:

A = dfrac{P times r times (1 + r)^n}{(1 + r)^n - 1}

Where:

r = dfrac{{Rate of interest}}{100}

**Calculations:**

Convert r into a fraction:

⇒ r = dfrac{5}{100} = 0.05

Substitute values into the formula:

⇒ A = dfrac{28700 times 0.05 times (1 + 0.05)²}{(1 + 0.05)² - 1}

⇒ A = dfrac{28700 times 0.05 times 1.1025}{1.1025 - 1}

⇒ A = dfrac{28700 times 0.05 times 1.1025}{0.1025}

⇒ A = dfrac{1582.0875}{0.1025}

⇒ A = ₹15,435

**∴ The annual equal payment required to discharge the debt is ₹15,435.**

